  "volume_summary": "Swatantra Newsletter No. 3, issued in January 1960 by the Central Office of the Swatantra Party, is an internal report on the party's early organisational expansion. It explains the newsletter's intended role as a link among regional units, records decisions taken at the Hyderabad meetings, announces the relocation of the Central Office to Bombay and the forthcoming national convention at Patna, and reports membership drives, district committees, public meetings, and local initiatives across the states.\n\nThe issue presents the party as a decentralised, service-oriented organisation seeking support among farmers, workers, students, teachers, professionals, small businesses, and rural communities. Its final annexure sets out a national-defence resolution responding to Chinese Communist aggression, calling for a review of non-alignment, closer regional security consultation, vigilance against infiltration, settlement of outstanding issues with Pakistan, and an end to ideological experimentation in domestic policy.",
